# FlightScope AI — API credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in the keys you have.
# The backend loads it automatically from the project root at import time.
# You need AT LEAST ONE OD-heat source (AirLabs, Aviationstack, or OpenSky
# history) for the analysis to produce route recommendations.
# All keys are optional; unconfigured sources are simply skipped.

# --- AirLabs (recommended, easy free tier) --------------------------------
# Sign up at https://airlabs.co/ → copy the API key.
AIRLABS_API_KEY=

# --- Aviationstack (free tier: ~100 requests/month) -----------------------
# Sign up at https://aviationstack.com/ → Dashboard → API Access Key.
AVIATIONSTACK_API_KEY=

# --- OpenSky Network (OAuth2 client credentials, for flight history) ------
# Create an account at https://opensky-network.org/, then create an API
# client (Account → API clients) to get a client id + secret.
OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=
OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Amadeus Self-Service (test environment) ------------------------------
# Register at https://developers.amadeus.com/ → create an app (test keys).
AMADEUS_CLIENT_ID=
AMADEUS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Note: Check24 (web scraping) additionally requires Playwright and is not
# used by the region-wide planner, so no key is needed here.
